# @NPM_NAME@

The Botlish native library `@LIBRARY@` as a React Native module: a Pure C++
TurboModule named `@MODULE@` (React Native's New Architecture, Hermes, JSI)
calling the library's C ABI. Generated by `botlish-react-native`
@TOOL_VERSION@ (`botlish tool ... react-native generate`) from
`@LIBRARY@.manifest.json`; do not edit: generate it again.

| | |
|---|---|
| Botlish library | `@LIBRARY@`, target `@TARGET@` (`@TRIPLE@`), C ABI version 1 |
| manifest | schema 2, SHA-256 `@MANIFEST_SHA@` |
| shared library | `native/android/arm64-v8a/lib@LIBRARY@.so`, SHA-256 `@SHARED_SHA@` |
| runtime ABI | `@RUNTIME_ABI@` |
| React Native | `@RN_RANGE@` (generated and tested against @RN_TESTED@), New Architecture, Hermes |
| Android | `arm64-v8a` only; minimum API @MIN_API@ (the library's own floor is @LIBRARY_API@) |
| iOS | not supported (no Botlish iOS library) |

## Install

    npm install ./@NPM_NAME@-@NPM_VERSION@.tgz

in a React Native @RN_MAJOR_MINOR@ app with the New Architecture, then build the
app for `arm64-v8a` alone (`reactNativeArchitectures=arm64-v8a` in
`android/gradle.properties`): the build stops with a message naming any
other ABI. Autolinking does the rest: the app's Codegen generates the
module's interface from `src/Native@MODULE@.ts`, its CMake build compiles
`cpp/` and links `lib@LIBRARY@.so`, which the APK carries.

## Use

```ts
import * as @MODULE@ from '@NPM_NAME@';
```

@API@

Each call runs synchronously on the JavaScript thread. A Botlish
instance of the library is created at the module's first call, on that
thread, and destroyed on that thread when the module goes (a reload) or the
thread ends. Arguments are checked before the library sees them
(`TypeError`, `RangeError`); what the library reports is a `BotlishError`
whose `identity` is the canonical Botlish name of a declared error.
